# Evidence: what the two full-chain PR jobs run out of
#
# Run 34278116323 on commit c866111, the first run with the sampler from
# scripts/ci/resource-monitor.sh in it:
#
#   job 102247036552  pr-test / full       exit 143
#   job 102240110409  pr-test / dind-full  exit 143
#
# Both died in the full box's `#64 exporting layers`, and both left the reading
# that the three earlier failures (run 34259552358) did not. Reproduced with:
#
#   gh api repos/link-foundation/box/actions/jobs/102247036552/logs
#   gh api repos/link-foundation/box/actions/jobs/102240110409/logs
#
# Read the two columns against each other. Disk: 11 MB consumed across the
# whole 4.5-minute export, 88 GB still free. Memory: 2.3 GB -> 18.8 GB
# committed (RAM plus swap), swap saturated at 3071 MB, still climbing ~2 GB
# per 30 s when the runner was taken down. The export runs out of memory while
# the disk sits idle, which is docker/buildx#1606 - reported against the docker
# driver since Docker 23.0, still open, with no daemon setting to turn it off -
# and it is why the fix (scripts/ci/ensure-swap.sh) spends the idle disk on
# swap rather than reclaiming more disk.
#
# For scale: the same two jobs passed on 2026-09-05 (run 33962512941, job
# 101300748685, `#63 exporting layers 171.1s done`) on the same runner image
# and the same Docker 28.0.4. What grew in between is what gets exported -
# commit 46f80a5 made the Lean boxes install a real toolchain, so the full
# box's `COPY --from=lean-stage /home/box/.elan` stopped copying a stub.

